ttps://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"First real kernel implementation attempt, intentionally DRAFT until pinned Rust compilation and the previously committed Asterinas guest CPU probe pass.\n\nChanges (exact source in branch):\n- Extend existing cgroup CPU controller with TSC-based period/runtime accounting, ancestor checks and throttle counters. Reconfiguration preserves already-used runtime.\n- Charge the common ClassScheduler current task on scheduler events; test eligibility in both real-time and fair queues; park throttled tasks and restore them from local idle ticks. Reuse cgroup state, not a parallel HOS2 ledger. No scheduler hot-injection or model calls.\n- Small A01 build-tool correction: remove `make --version | head -1` / `gcc --version | head -1` pipes under `set -o pipefail` after observing SIGPIPE 141 before any kernel compilation.\n\n**Not claimed:** verified CPU enforcement, SMP correctness, parent/scheduler migration correctness, kernel build, Hepta effects, or API stabilization. We will retain raw build/boot/probe evidence, fix compile and semantic issues here, and not merge if regressions exist. Work is restricted to disposable QEMU and isolated source worktree; no production host cgroup, disk, services or firmware changed. Root README remains 0 bytes.\n\nBaseline failing case in merged tests: 1% `cpu.max=1000 100000` written/read back but guest still used ~998ms CPU per 1000ms wall. Success requires low actual CPU consumption, bounded error and no deadlocks/panics in the **modified** kernel with independent probe.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T10:42:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T00:51:29Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"83f5fc7277fe5deb53e57d47813fb8a708de06d8","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewer